### Description

`Weight#count` of `IndexSortSortedNumericDocValuesRangeQuery` can be lower than the number of hits when the primary sort field is multi-valued.

The scorer only uses the index sort optimization when `DocValues.unwrapSingleton` returns non-null. `count()` does not check this. If the missing value is outside the range, it runs the binary search on the value selected by the sort, for example the minimum. A document matches when any of its values is in range, so a document whose selected value is outside the range is not counted. Document blocks are not involved.

Ascending `LONG` sort with `MIN`, missing value `Long.MAX_VALUE`, one document with the values 5 and 25, range `[20, 30]`. The search returns the document and `IndexSearcher#count` returns 0. It is the same with points and with a descending sort.

Suggested fix: in `count()`, return the fallback count as soon as `unwrapSingleton` returns null, as the scorer does.

#### Reproduction

Save as `MultiValuedRepro.java` and run `java -cp <lucene-core jar> MultiValuedRepro.java`. It checks that the count is 1 and compares it with the count of the fallback query alone, which is correct here. It throws an `AssertionError` on the versions below.

```java
import org.apache.lucene.document.Document;
import org.apache.lucene.document.SortedNumericDocValuesField;
import org.apache.lucene.index.DirectoryReader;
import org.apache.lucene.index.IndexWriter;
import org.apache.lucene.index.IndexWriterConfig;
import org.apache.lucene.search.IndexSearcher;
import org.apache.lucene.search.IndexSortSortedNumericDocValuesRangeQuery;
import org.apache.lucene.search.Query;
import org.apache.lucene.search.Sort;
import org.apache.lucene.search.SortField;
import org.apache.lucene.search.SortedNumericSelector;
import org.apache.lucene.search.SortedNumericSortField;
import org.apache.lucene.store.ByteBuffersDirectory;
import org.apache.lucene.store.Directory;

public class MultiValuedRepro {

  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    SortField sortField =
        new SortedNumericSortField(
            "ts", SortField.Type.LONG, false, SortedNumericSelector.Type.MIN, Long.MAX_VALUE);
    IndexWriterConfig config = new IndexWriterConfig().setIndexSort(new Sort(sortField));
    try (Directory dir = new ByteBuffersDirectory();
        IndexWriter writer = new IndexWriter(dir, config)) {
      Document document = new Document();
      document.add(new SortedNumericDocValuesField("ts", 5));
      document.add(new SortedNumericDocValuesField("ts", 25));
      writer.addDocument(document);
      try (DirectoryReader reader = DirectoryReader.open(writer)) {
        IndexSearcher searcher = new IndexSearcher(reader);
        Query reference = SortedNumericDocValuesField.newSlowRangeQuery("ts", 20, 30);
        Query query = new IndexSortSortedNumericDocValuesRangeQuery("ts", 20, 30, reference);
        int referenceCount = searcher.count(reference);
        int actual = searcher.count(query);
        if (actual != 1 || referenceCount != 1) {
          throw new AssertionError(
              "expected count 1 but got " + actual + " (reference " + referenceCount + ")");
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Version and environment details

Lucene 10.4.0, 10.5.2, a 10.6.0 snapshot and `main` at `bc0d7097dc`. Java 25.

