### Description

The lite-pull assign example `example/src/main/java/org/apache/rocketmq/example/simple/LitePullConsumerAssign.java` crashes for topics with a single message queue:

```java
Collection<MessageQueue> mqSet = litePullConsumer.fetchMessageQueues("TopicTest");
List<MessageQueue> list = new ArrayList<>(mqSet);
List<MessageQueue> assignList = new ArrayList<>();
for (int i = 0; i < list.size() / 2; i++) {
    assignList.add(list.get(i));
}
litePullConsumer.assign(assignList);
litePullConsumer.seek(assignList.get(0), 10);
```

`list.size() / 2` is integer division. With 1 queue the loop body never executes, `assignList` stays empty, and `assignList.get(0)` throws `IndexOutOfBoundsException`. A single-queue topic is a perfectly legal setup (fresh topics, small test clusters), so the example is unusable there. (With 3 queues it also assigns only 1 queue — arguably not "half" either.)

### Expected behavior

The example should assign at least one queue whenever the topic has queues — e.g. use ceiling division `(list.size() + 1) / 2` so 1 queue → 1 assigned, 3 → 2, 4 → 2 — instead of crashing on `assignList.get(0)`.

