### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`8a10a2f4822`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should report a syntax error as the Firebird server does, with SQL error code -104 ([`isc_sqlerr`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1260-L1275)) and the position of the error.

### Actual behavior

The proxy answers both statements with an error without SQL error code -104 and without the position.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT FROM T_PLAIN` | Error [`isc_dsql_token_unk_err`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1269-L1274) "Dynamic SQL Error; SQL error code = -104; Token unknown - line 1, column 8; FROM" | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input 'FROM'" |
| `SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE` | Error [`isc_command_end_err2`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1262-L1265) "Dynamic SQL Error; SQL error code = -104; Unexpected end of command - line 1, column 24" | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '<EOF>'" |

So through the proxy an application gets only `isc_dsql_error` with a text for a syntax error, without the `isc_sqlerr` -104 and [`isc_dsql_token_unk_err`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1269-L1274) or [`isc_command_end_err2`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1262-L1265) items that the Firebird server sends after it. Jaybird therefore reports the error code `isc_dsql_error` instead of `isc_dsql_token_unk_err` or `isc_command_end_err2`, and the application cannot show the user where the error is.

### Reason analysis

- [`SQLParserErrorListener#syntaxError`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/parser/sql/engine/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/core/database/parser/SQLParserErrorListener.java#L45-L47) keeps the offending token and the line of a syntax error but drops the column, and when the second parsing phase is cancelled, [`SQLParserExecutor#twoPhaseParse`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/parser/sql/engine/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/core/database/parser/SQLParserExecutor.java#L69-L70) keeps only the SQL text. [`ShardingSphereSQLParserEngine#getException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/infra/parser/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/parser/ShardingSphereSQLParserEngine.java#L64-L68) copies the token and the line into [`DialectSQLParsingException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/exception/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/core/exception/syntax/sql/DialectSQLParsingException.java#L29). [`MySQLDialectExceptionMapper`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/exception/dialect/mysql/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/mysql/mapper/MySQLDialectExceptionMapper.java#L76-L79) passes them to the client, but [`FirebirdDialectExceptionMapper#convert`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/exception/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/firebird/mapper/FirebirdDialectExceptionMapper.java#L95-L97) uses only the text and maps the exception to [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250), without [`isc_sqlerr`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L117) -104 and without the line and column.
- [`FirebirdStatusVector`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/err/FirebirdStatusVector.java#L43-L47) is built from one `SQLException`, that is one error code with string arguments, optionally followed by `isc_random` ([`FirebirdErrorSegmentResolver`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/err/FirebirdErrorSegmentResolver.java#L60-L79)). It cannot carry what the Firebird server sends for a syntax error, that is `isc_dsql_error`, `isc_sqlerr` with the number -104, `isc_dsql_token_unk_err` or `isc_command_end_err2` with the line and the column as numbers, and `isc_random` with the token ([`Parser.cpp`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1260-L1275)).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SyntaxErrorCode {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // Firebird server: "SELECT FROM T_PLAIN -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; SQL error code = -104; Token unknown - line 1, column 8; FROM [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544634]";
            // proxy: "SELECT FROM T_PLAIN -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input 'FROM' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT FROM T_PLAIN");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; SQL error code = -104; Unexpected end of command - line 1, column 24 [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544851]";
            // proxy: "SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '<EOF>' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

