- [`FirebirdDatabaseMetaData#getTransactionOption`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/connector/firebird/metadata/database/FirebirdDatabaseMetaData.java#L60-L63) sets [`DDLCommitPolicy.COMMIT_CURRENT_TRANSACTION`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/connector/core/metadata/database/metadata/option/transaction/DDLCommitPolicy.java#L25) for Firebird.
- With auto-commit off, [`StandardDatabaseProxyConnector#doExecute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/StandardDatabaseProxyConnector.java#L241-L244) commits the backend transaction with [`ProxyBackendTransactionManager#commit`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/jdbc/transaction/ProxyBackendTransactionManager.java#L108-L120) after every DDL statement because of this policy ([`StandardDatabaseProxyConnector#isCurrentTransactionCommitRequired`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/StandardDatabaseProxyConnector.java#L256-L260)). The client keeps its transaction, the statements after the DDL run in the next backend transaction, and [`rollback()`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L412) undoes only them.
- The commit after DDL was added with Firebird support, in ShardingSphere-JDBC by #33773 and in ShardingSphere-Proxy by #35937 (the flag became a dialect option in #33783 and `DDLCommitPolicy` in #39160). In the proxy it runs right before the [metadata refresh](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/StandardDatabaseProxyConnector.java#L245-L249), which loads the new table through another connection of the data source ([`FirebirdMetaDataLoader#load`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/connector/firebird/metadata/data/loader/FirebirdMetaDataLoader.java#L43), [`TableMetaDataLoader`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/connector/core/metadata/data/loader/type/TableMetaDataLoader.java#L86)); that connection does not see DDL that is not committed yet. ShardingSphere-JDBC does the same in [`DriverJDBCPushDownExecuteUpdateExecutor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/jdbc/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/driver/executor/engine/pushdown/jdbc/DriverJDBCPushDownExecuteUpdateExecutor.java#L112-L119), but only when a refresh is needed, while the proxy commits after every DDL statement.
- So the commit cannot simply be removed. The open pull request #39882 defers the metadata refresh to the commit for PostgreSQL but keeps the commit for [`DDLCommitPolicy.COMMIT_CURRENT_TRANSACTION`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/connector/core/metadata/database/metadata/option/transaction/DDLCommitPolicy.java#L25); with such a deferred refresh Firebird could use `DDLCommitPolicy.NO_ADDITIONAL_COMMIT`.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. The table T_AUDIT_DDL_TX must not exist before each run. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;

public class DdlInTransaction {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8891 AND 8892");
        dropTable();
        ddlInTransaction();
        dropTable();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8891 AND 8892");
    }

    // Firebird server and proxy: "insert ID = 8891: 1 row", "create table: success", "insert ID = 8892: 1 row", "rollback: success";
    // Firebird server: "ID = 8891: the row is not saved", "ID = 8892: the row is not saved", "T_AUDIT_DDL_TX: the table does not exist";
    // proxy: "ID = 8891: the row is saved", "ID = 8892: the row is not saved", "T_AUDIT_DDL_TX: the table exists"
    static void ddlInTransaction() throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD);
             Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            System.out.println("insert ID = 8891: " + statement.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8891, 'before ddl')") + " row");
            statement.executeUpdate("CREATE TABLE T_AUDIT_DDL_TX (ID INTEGER)");
            System.out.println("create table: success");
            System.out.println("insert ID = 8892: " + statement.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8892, 'after ddl')") + " row");
            connection.rollback();
            System.out.println("rollback: success");
        }
        printRow(8891);
        printRow(8892);
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'T_AUDIT_DDL_TX'")) {
            resultSet.next();
            System.out.println("T_AUDIT_DDL_TX: " + (0 < resultSet.getInt(1) ? "the table exists" : "the table does not exist"));
        }
    }

    // Drops the table through the URL under test, so that the proxy does not keep it in its metadata.
    // The table may not exist, then the error is ignored.
    static void dropTable() {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute("DROP TABLE T_AUDIT_DDL_TX");
        } catch (final SQLException ignored) {
            // the table does not exist
        }
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is not saved"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
