### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should decode text that a client sends on a connection with the character set ([`isc_dpb_lc_ctype`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/jrd.cpp#L7093-L7095)) [`SJIS_0208`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/IntlManager.cpp#L115) as Shift-JIS, as the Firebird server does, and store the same text.

### Actual behavior

The statement succeeds, but the proxy stores replacement characters instead of the text.

The same statement was executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, and the bytes of NAME were read directly from the server with [`CAST`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L8567-L8570) to the character set [`OCTETS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/IntlManager.cpp#L107):

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8903, '日本語')` on a connection with [`encoding`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L55)`=SJIS_0208` | Success, NAME is stored as `e697a5e69cace8aa9e`, the text `日本語` in UTF-8 | Success, NAME is stored as `efbfbdefbfbdefbfbd7befbfbdefbfbd`, replacement characters U+FFFD and `{` instead of the text |

So through the proxy an application on a [`SJIS_0208`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/IntlManager.cpp#L115) connection gets replacement characters in the database instead of its text, and no error tells it that something went wrong.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdAuthenticationEngine#parseAttachCharset`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L103-L112) maps the connection character set ([`isc_dpb_lc_ctype`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/jrd.cpp#L7093-L7095)) to a Java charset with [`FirebirdCharacterSets#findCharacterSet`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/executor/variable/charset/FirebirdCharacterSets.java#L119-L123). [`FirebirdPrepareStatementPacket`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementPacket.java#L59) reads the SQL text with [`FirebirdPacketPayload#readString`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/payload/FirebirdPacketPayload.java#L231-L233), which decodes it with this charset, and the proxy passes it to the backend as a Java string.
- [`FirebirdCharacterSets.SJIS_0208`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/executor/variable/charset/FirebirdCharacterSets.java#L73) is `ISO-2022-JP`, while [`SJIS_0208`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/IntlManager.cpp#L115) in the Firebird server is [Shift-JIS](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/intl/charsets.h#L33). Jaybird uses the Java charset `MS932` for `SJIS_0208` ([`DefaultEncodingSet`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/encodings/DefaultEncodingSet.java#L60)).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server in a database with the default character set UTF8:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statement from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above the method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.util.HexFormat;
import java.util.Properties;

public class ConnectionCharsetMapping {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 8903");
        sjisConnection();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 8903");
    }

    // Firebird server: "ID = 8903: success, NAME is stored as e697a5e69cace8aa9e";
    // proxy: "ID = 8903: success, NAME is stored as efbfbdefbfbdefbfbd7befbfbdefbfbd"
    static void sjisConnection() throws SQLException {
        // Jaybird sends the text in Shift-JIS
        insert("SJIS_0208", 8903, "INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8903, '日本語')");
    }

    // Executes the statement on a connection with the given connection character set
    // and reads the stored bytes directly on the Firebird server
    static void insert(final String encoding, final int id, final String sql) throws SQLException {
        Properties properties = new Properties();
        properties.setProperty("user", USER);
        properties.setProperty("password", PASSWORD);
        properties.setProperty("wireCrypt", "DISABLED");
        properties.setProperty("encoding", encoding);
        String result;
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, properties);
             Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            statement.executeUpdate(sql);
            result = "success";
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            result = ex.getMessage();
        }
        System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + result + ", NAME is stored as " + storedBytes(id));
    }

    // Reads the bytes of NAME directly on the Firebird server
    static String storedBytes(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery(
                     "SELECT CAST(NAME AS VARCHAR(80) CHARACTER SET OCTETS) FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            return resultSet.next() ? HexFormat.of().formatHex(resultSet.getBytes(1)) : "nothing, the row is lost";
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

