### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should return and save [`TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4853-L4859) values with their time zone, as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy returns [`TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4853-L4859) values in another time zone and saves a [`TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4853-L4859) parameter without its time zone.

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, the values were read with [`getString`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBResultSet.java#L452-L454), and the saved rows were read directly from the Firebird server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911`, the value is `2026-10-15 10:11:12.3456 -05:30` | `2026-10-15T10:11:12.345600-05:30` | `2026-10-15T21:41:12.345600+06:00` |
| `SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8912`, the value is `2026-10-15 10:11:12 America/Sao_Paulo` | `2026-10-15T10:11:12-03:00` | `2026-10-15T08:11:12-05:00` |
| Insert a row with ID = 8913 and TSZ = `2026-10-15T10:11:12-05:30`, an `OffsetDateTime` parameter of [`setObject`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBPreparedStatement.java#L312-L314) | Success, the row is saved with the time `10:11:12.0000 -05:30` | Success, the row is saved with the time `15:41:12.0000 +00:00`, in the time zone of the proxy JVM (UTC) |

So through the proxy an application gets [`TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4853-L4859) values in a time zone it did not write and saves them in the time zone of the proxy instead of their own.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdTimestampTZBinaryProtocolValue#write`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdTimestampTZBinaryProtocolValue.java#L37-L43) writes the offset in minutes (-330 for `-05:30`) to the time zone field of a result value. The Firebird server [writes](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/xdr.cpp#L295-L303) the time zone id there, and the id of an offset is the offset plus 1439 ([`displacementToOffsetZone`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/TimeZoneUtil.cpp#L1171-L1174), [`ONE_DAY`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/TimeZoneUtil.cpp#L302)), so the client reads the same moment in another time zone.
- [`FirebirdTimestampTZBinaryProtocolValue#read`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdTimestampTZBinaryProtocolValue.java#L32-L35) reads a parameter with [`FirebirdDateTimeUtils#getDateTimeWithOffset`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/util/FirebirdDateTimeUtils.java#L207-L210), which ignores the time zone field (the comment [`// TODO add time zone support`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/util/FirebirdDateTimeUtils.java#L208)) and returns a `Timestamp` with the UTC date and time. The backend driver then saves this date and time in the default time zone of the proxy JVM ([`AbstractWithTimeZoneField#setTimestamp`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/field/AbstractWithTimeZoneField.java#L132-L141)), so the value loses its time zone, and when the proxy JVM does not run in UTC, it is also saved as another moment.
- Even after these fixes a named time zone such as `America/Sao_Paulo` is returned as an offset, because [`StandardDatabaseProxyConnector#getRowData`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/StandardDatabaseProxyConnector.java#L360) reads the value with `getObject` ([`JDBCStreamQueryResult#getValue`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/executor/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/executor/sql/execute/result/query/impl/driver/jdbc/type/stream/JDBCStreamQueryResult.java#L127)), and Jaybird returns an `OffsetDateTime` ([`FBTimestampTzField#getObject`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/field/FBTimestampTzField.java#L41-L43)).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table and the rows on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_DTZ (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, TMZ TIME WITH TIME ZONE, TSZ TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE);
INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8911, TIME '10:11:12.3456 +03:00', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12.3456 -05:30');
INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8912, TIME '23:59:59 Europe/Moscow', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12 America/Sao_Paulo');
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.PreparedStatement;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.time.OffsetDateTime;
import java.time.OffsetTime;
import java.time.ZoneOffset;

public class TimeZoneTypes {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to write and read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID BETWEEN 8911 AND 8913");
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8911, TIME '10:11:12.3456 +03:00', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12.3456 -05:30')");
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8912, TIME '23:59:59 Europe/Moscow', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12 America/Sao_Paulo')");
        // One connection per case
        selectTimestampWithOffset();
        selectTimestampWithNamedZone();
        insertTimestamp();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID BETWEEN 8911 AND 8913");
    }

    // Firebird server: "SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911: 2026-10-15T10:11:12.345600-05:30";
    // proxy: "SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911: 2026-10-15T21:41:12.345600+06:00"
    static void selectTimestampWithOffset() {
        printSelect("SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911");
    }

    // Firebird server: "SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8912: 2026-10-15T10:11:12-03:00";
    // proxy: "SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8912: 2026-10-15T08:11:12-05:00"
    static void selectTimestampWithNamedZone() {
        printSelect("SELECT TSZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8912");
    }

    // Firebird server: "Insert ID = 8913: success", "ID = 8913: 10:11:12.0000 -05:30";
    // proxy: "Insert ID = 8913: success", "ID = 8913: 15:41:12.0000 +00:00"
    static void insertTimestamp() throws SQLException {
        insert(8913, "TSZ", OffsetDateTime.of(2026, 10, 15, 10, 11, 12, 0, ZoneOffset.ofHoursMinutes(-5, -30)));
        printSaved(8913, "TSZ");
    }

    // Executes the query through the proxy and prints the value as a string
    static void printSelect(final String sql) {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD);
             Statement statement = connection.createStatement();
             ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery(sql)) {
            resultSet.next();
            System.out.println(sql + ": " + resultSet.getString(1));
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + ": " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // Inserts the row through the proxy with the value as a parameter
    static void insert(final int id, final String column, final Object value) {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD);
             PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, " + column + ") VALUES (?, ?)")) {
            statement.setInt(1, id);
            statement.setObject(2, value);
            statement.executeUpdate();
            System.out.println("Insert ID = " + id + ": success");
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println("Insert ID = " + id + ": " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // Reads the time and the time zone of the saved value directly on the Firebird server
    static void printSaved(final int id, final String column) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery(
                     "SELECT CAST(CAST(" + column + " AS TIME WITH TIME ZONE) AS VARCHAR(60)) FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? resultSet.getString(1) : "the row is not saved"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

