### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should apply the transaction parameter [`isc_tpb_read`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/tra.cpp#L3137-L3161) of [`op_transaction`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5147-L5148) as the Firebird server does and reject writes in a read-only transaction.

### Actual behavior

The proxy does not apply this parameter and writes in a read-only transaction.

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, and the rows were read directly from the server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`setReadOnly(true)`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L601-L613) ([`isc_tpb_read`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/tra.cpp#L3137-L3161)), insert a row with ID = 8951, commit | Error [`isc_read_only_trans`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/rlck.cpp#L70-L73) "attempted update during read-only transaction", the commit succeeds, the row is not saved | Success, the commit succeeds, the row is saved |

So through the proxy an application saves rows in a read-only transaction, while the Firebird server rejects the insert.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdStartTransactionPacket#isReadOnly`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/transaction/FirebirdStartTransactionPacket.java#L57-L59) reads [`isc_tpb_read`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/tra.cpp#L3137-L3161), and [`FirebirdStartTransactionCommandExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/transaction/FirebirdStartTransactionCommandExecutor.java#L44-L51) puts it into [`ConnectionSession`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/session/ConnectionSession.java#L44).
- [`ProxyDatabaseConnectionManager#replayTransactionOptions`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/ProxyDatabaseConnectionManager.java#L227-L235) calls [`setReadOnly(true)`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L568-L578) and then [`setTransactionIsolation`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L611-L619) on the connection to the Firebird server. [`getIsolationLevel`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/transaction/FirebirdStartTransactionPacket.java#L76) always returns a level, so the isolation level is always set. Jaybird, which the proxy uses for this connection, replaces the whole TPB in [`FBManagedConnection#setTransactionIsolation`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/xca/FBManagedConnection.java#L1122-L1130), and the read-only flag that [`FBManagedConnection#setReadOnly`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/xca/FBManagedConnection.java#L1147-L1149) has set is lost.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above the method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;

public class TransactionParameters {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 8951");
                readOnly();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 8951");
    }

    // Firebird server: "READ ONLY, insert: attempted update during read-only transaction [SQLState:25006, ISC error code:335544361]", "READ ONLY, commit: success",
    // "ID = 8951: the row is not saved";
    // proxy: "READ ONLY, insert: success", "READ ONLY, commit: success", "ID = 8951: the row is saved"
    static void readOnly() throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            // Jaybird sends isc_tpb_read in the TPB of op_transaction
            connection.setReadOnly(true);
            System.out.println("READ ONLY, insert: " + execute(connection, "INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8951, 'read only')"));
            connection.commit();
            System.out.println("READ ONLY, commit: success");
        }
        printRow(8951);
    }

    static String execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            statement.executeUpdate(sql);
            return "success";
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            return ex.getMessage();
        }
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is not saved"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

