### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute [`SELECT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5781-L5792) with [`FOR UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5795-L5798), [`FOR UPDATE OF`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5801-L5804) and [`WITH LOCK`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5807-L5810) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, in one transaction with auto-commit off, after inserting a row with ID = 6701:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE` | The row with ID = 6701 | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE, null" |
| `SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK` | The row with ID = 6701 | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK, null" |
| `SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK` | The row with ID = 6701 | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK, null" |

So through the proxy an application cannot lock the rows it reads ([`WITH LOCK`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5807-L5810)) and cannot open a cursor for positioned updates ([`FOR UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5795-L5798)).

### Reason analysis

- The rule [`select`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L71-L73) of the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere has no [`FOR UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5795-L5798) and no [`WITH LOCK`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5807-L5810), so the proxy rejects these statements with a syntax error.
- [`FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor#visitSelect`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor.java#L259-L266) would also have to create a `LockSegment`. Only with it ShardingSphere routes a locking read to the primary data source ([`QualifiedReadwriteSplittingPrimaryDataSourceRouter`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/features/readwrite-splitting/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/readwritesplitting/route/qualified/type/QualifiedReadwriteSplittingPrimaryDataSourceRouter.java#L48-L49)) and does not merge it into `UNION ALL` ([`RouteSQLRewriteEngine`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/rewrite/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/rewrite/engine/RouteSQLRewriteEngine.java#L115-L116)).
- The Firebird server reports `FOR UPDATE` as [`isc_info_sql_stmt_select_for_upd`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/StmtNodes.cpp#L8332-L8336), while [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L172-L173) always reports `isc_info_sql_stmt_select`. [`SELECT_FOR_UPD`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/info/type/sql/FirebirdSQLInfoReturnValue.java#L44) is declared but not used.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Turn auto-commit off, execute `INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (6701, 'before')` and then the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" in the same transaction through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SelectLockClauses {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to delete the rows of the example directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 6701 AND 6709");
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            // Firebird server: "INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (6701, 'before') -> update count 1";
            // proxy: "INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (6701, 'before') -> update count 1"
            execute(connection, "INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (6701, 'before')");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE -> ID INTEGER, NAME VARCHAR(20): 6701, before";
            // proxy: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax:
            // SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK -> ID INTEGER, NAME VARCHAR(20): 6701, before";
            // proxy: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax:
            // SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 WITH LOCK");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK -> ID INTEGER, NAME VARCHAR(20): 6701, before";
            // proxy: "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK -> error: Dynamic SQL Error;
            // You have an error in your SQL syntax: SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 FOR UPDATE OF NAME WITH LOCK");
            connection.commit();
        }
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 6701 AND 6709");
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
