body_text:
### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute the session management statements ([`SET TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5523-L5531), [`SET BIND`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5405-L5407), [`SET DECFLOAT ROUND`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5391-L5393), [`SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5501-L5502), [`SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5499-L5500), [`ALTER SESSION RESET`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5371-L5373)) as the Firebird server does, or reject them with an error, but not ignore them.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow'` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow', null" |
| `SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY, null" |
| `SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING, null" |
| `SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10, null" |
| `SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600, null" |
| `ALTER SESSION RESET` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input 'ALTERSESSION'" |

So through the proxy an application cannot change the session time zone, the data type bindings, the rounding mode or the timeouts, and cannot reset the session.

### Reason analysis

- [`execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/autogen/FirebirdStatement.g4#L22-L55) in the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere has no session management statements ([`mng_statement`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L915-L926) of the Firebird server), and [`setTransaction`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/TCLStatement.g4#L22-L24) is the only statement in it that starts with SET.
- [`FirebirdAdminExecutorCreator#create`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/FirebirdAdminExecutorCreator.java#L38-L47) handles [`SetStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dal/SetStatement.java#L32) and [`ShowStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dal/ShowStatement.java#L27), but the Firebird parser never produces these statements.
- A grammar rule alone is not enough. [`FirebirdSetVariableAdminExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/executor/FirebirdSetVariableAdminExecutor.java#L42-L48) records a variable with [`SessionVariableRecordExecutor#recordVariable`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/SessionVariableRecordExecutor.java#L47-L54), which keeps it only if a [`ReplayedSessionVariableProvider`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/ReplayedSessionVariableProvider.java) of the database type accepts it. Only MySQL has one ([`MySQLReplayedSessionVariableProvider`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/mysql/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/mysql/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/MySQLReplayedSessionVariableProvider.java)), and [`RequiredSessionVariableRecorder#toSetSQLs`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/session/RequiredSessionVariableRecorder.java#L64-L77) replays variables only for MySQL and PostgreSQL. So once parsed, these statements would be answered with success and discarded.
- The statements need different support. `SET TIME ZONE`, `SET DECFLOAT ROUND` and `SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT` have to be replayed on the backend connections. The proxy describes and encodes the columns itself, so `SET BIND` has to change the description in the Firebird frontend. `SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT` and `ALTER SESSION RESET` act on the client connection, which the Firebird frontend owns.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

2. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SessionStatements {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // Firebird server: "SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow' -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow' -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow', null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow'");
            // Firebird server: "SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SET BIND OF DECFLOAT TO LEGACY");
            // Firebird server: "SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SET DECFLOAT ROUND CEILING");
            // Firebird server: "SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10 -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10 -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT 10");
            // Firebird server: "SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600 -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600 -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600, null [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT 600");
            // Firebird server: "ALTER SESSION RESET -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "ALTER SESSION RESET -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input 'ALTERSESSION' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "ALTER SESSION RESET");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
