### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute the session management statements ([`SET TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5523-L5531), [`SET BIND`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5405-L5407), [`SET DECFLOAT ROUND`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5391-L5393), [`SET STATEMENT TIMEOUT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5501-L5502), [`SET SESSION IDLE TIMEOUT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5499-L5500), [`ALTER SESSION RESET`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5371-L5373)) as the Firebird server does, or reject them with an error, but not ignore them.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow'` | Success | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SET TIME ZONE 'Europe/Moscow', null" |
