- [`FirebirdAdminExecutorCreator#create`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/FirebirdAdminExecutorCreator.java#L38-L47) handles [`SetStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dal/SetStatement.java#L32) and [`ShowStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dal/ShowStatement.java#L27), but the Firebird parser never produces these statements.
- A grammar rule alone is not enough. [`FirebirdSetVariableAdminExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/firebird/handler/admin/executor/FirebirdSetVariableAdminExecutor.java#L42-L48) records a variable with [`SessionVariableRecordExecutor#recordVariable`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/SessionVariableRecordExecutor.java#L47-L54), which keeps it only if a [`ReplayedSessionVariableProvider`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/ReplayedSessionVariableProvider.java) of the database type accepts it. Only MySQL has one ([`MySQLReplayedSessionVariableProvider`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/dialect/mysql/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/mysql/handler/admin/executor/variable/session/MySQLReplayedSessionVariableProvider.java)), and [`RequiredSessionVariableRecorder#toSetSQLs`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/session/RequiredSessionVariableRecorder.java#L64-L77) replays variables only for MySQL and PostgreSQL. So once parsed, these statements would be answered with success and discarded.
