body_text:
### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute these statements on the system tables and describe their columns as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes some system table columns with a wrong type and does not know some system tables and columns of Firebird 5.0.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, and the column types were read with [`getColumnTypeName`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBResultSetMetaData.java#L225):

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT MON$PAGE_SIZE FROM MON$DATABASE` | One row: 8192, type [`INTEGER`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/fields.h#L138) | One row: 8192, type [`SMALLINT`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables/mon$database.yaml#L27-L33) |
| `SELECT RDB$SQL_SECURITY FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'T_PLAIN'` | One row: NULL, type [`BOOLEAN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/fields.h#L197) | One row: NULL, type [`SMALLINT`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables/rdb$relations.yaml#L139-L145) |
| `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$KEYWORDS` | One row: 499, the [keywords](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/KeywordsTable.cpp#L45-L58) of Firebird 5.0.4 | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Table or view 'RDB$KEYWORDS' does not exist." |
| `SELECT RDB$COLLATION_ID FROM RDB$FIELDS WHERE RDB$FIELD_NAME = 'RDB$RELATION_NAME'` | One row: 0 | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column 'RDB$COLLATION_ID' in 'field list'." |
| `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$PACKAGES` | One row: 3 | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Table or view 'RDB$PACKAGES' does not exist." |

So through the proxy an application gets wrong types for system table columns and cannot read the system tables and columns of Firebird 5.0 that the proxy does not know.

### Reason analysis

- The proxy takes the schemas of the system tables from the YAML files in [`system_tables`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/tree/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables), not from the server. [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#processReturnValues`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L248-L253) describes the columns of a system table from these files. The open pull request #40191 changes this code to describe the lengths of text columns of system tables, but the types still come from these files, and it adds no tables or columns.
- These files differ from Firebird 5.0 ([`relations.h`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h), [`fields.h`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/fields.h)). Six columns have a wrong `dataType`: [`MON$PAGE_SIZE`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables/mon$database.yaml#L27-L33) of `MON$DATABASE` and [`RDB$SQL_SECURITY`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables/rdb$relations.yaml#L139-L145) of `RDB$RELATIONS` have `5`, `RDB$TRANSACTION_ID` of `RDB$TRANSACTIONS` has `4`, `RDB$ENGINE_NAME` of `RDB$PROCEDURES` and `RDB$SYSTEM_FLAG` of `RDB$EXCEPTIONS` have `2004`, `SEC$MAP_FROM` of `SEC$GLOBAL_AUTH_MAPPING` has `12`. Six columns are missing: [`RDB$COLLATION_ID`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L72) in [`rdb$fields.yaml`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/connector/dialect/firebird/src/main/resources/schema/firebird/system_tables/rdb$fields.yaml), `MON$SESSION_TIMEZONE` and `MON$PARALLEL_WORKERS` of `MON$ATTACHMENTS`, `MON$COMPILED_STATEMENT_ID` of `MON$STATEMENTS` and `MON$CALL_STACK`, `SEC$DESCRIPTION` of `SEC$GLOBAL_AUTH_MAPPING`. Six system tables have no file: [`RDB$KEYWORDS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L746), [`RDB$PACKAGES`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L635), [`RDB$PUBLICATIONS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L721), [`RDB$PUBLICATION_TABLES`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L730), [`RDB$LOG_FILES`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L362) and [`MON$COMPILED_STATEMENTS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/relations.h#L752).
- [`SimpleTableSegmentBinder#checkTableExists`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/segment/dml/from/type/SimpleTableSegmentBinder.java#L378) rejects a table without a file with [`TableNotFoundException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/common/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/exception/kernel/metadata/TableNotFoundException.java#L26-L31), and [`ColumnSegmentBinder#bind`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/segment/dml/expression/type/ColumnSegmentBinder.java#L111-L112) rejects a column that is not in the file with [`ColumnNotFoundException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/common/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/exception/kernel/metadata/ColumnNotFoundException.java#L26-L31).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SystemTableSchemas {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // Firebird server: "SELECT MON$PAGE_SIZE FROM MON$DATABASE -> MON$PAGE_SIZE INTEGER: 8192";
            // proxy: "SELECT MON$PAGE_SIZE FROM MON$DATABASE -> MON$PAGE_SIZE SMALLINT: 8192"
            execute(connection, "SELECT MON$PAGE_SIZE FROM MON$DATABASE");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT RDB$SQL_SECURITY FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'T_PLAIN' -> RDB$SQL_SECURITY BOOLEAN: null";
            // proxy: "SELECT RDB$SQL_SECURITY FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'T_PLAIN' -> RDB$SQL_SECURITY SMALLINT: null"
            execute(connection, "SELECT RDB$SQL_SECURITY FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'T_PLAIN'");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$KEYWORDS -> COUNT BIGINT: 499";
            // proxy: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$KEYWORDS -> error: Table or view 'RDB$KEYWORDS' does not exist. [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$KEYWORDS");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT RDB$COLLATION_ID FROM RDB$FIELDS WHERE RDB$FIELD_NAME = 'RDB$RELATION_NAME' -> RDB$COLLATION_ID SMALLINT: 0";
            // proxy: "SELECT RDB$COLLATION_ID FROM RDB$FIELDS WHERE RDB$FIELD_NAME = 'RDB$RELATION_NAME'
            // -> error: Unknown column 'RDB$COLLATION_ID' in 'field list'. [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT RDB$COLLATION_ID FROM RDB$FIELDS WHERE RDB$FIELD_NAME = 'RDB$RELATION_NAME'");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$PACKAGES -> COUNT BIGINT: 3";
            // proxy: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$PACKAGES -> error: Table or view 'RDB$PACKAGES' does not exist. [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$PACKAGES");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
