| `SELECT CAST('2026-10-15 10:11:12' AS DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Success, the column CAST of type [TIMESTAMP](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4811-L4818) with the value 2026-10-15 10:11:12 | Error [`isc_convert_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/cvt.cpp#L2282) "conversion error from string "2026-10-15 10:11:12"" |
| `INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (7302, "after")` | Success, the row is saved | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column 'after' in 'unknown clause'.", the row is lost |

So an application that works in SQL dialect 1 cannot use string constants in double quotes and the dialect 1 [`DATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4806-L4827) type through the proxy, although the Firebird server executes these statements.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdPrepareStatementPacket`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementPacket.java#L58) reads the dialect of the client into [`sqlDialect`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementPacket.java#L42), but nothing in the Firebird protocol and frontend modules uses it.
- In dialect 1 the Firebird server reads a string in double quotes as a string constant ([lexer](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L519-L577)). The Firebird lexer of ShardingSphere reads it only as an identifier ([`IDENTIFIER_`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/Literals.g4#L22-L25)), whatever the dialect of the client. So [`ColumnSegmentBinder#bind`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/segment/dml/expression/type/ColumnSegmentBinder.java#L111-L112) looks for the columns abc and after and throws [`ColumnNotFoundException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/common/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/exception/kernel/metadata/ColumnNotFoundException.java#L31).
- The proxy executes the statement on its backend connection, which has the default dialect 3 of Jaybird ([`DEFAULT_DIALECT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyConstants.java#L46)). In dialect 3 [`DATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4821-L4825) is a date without time, and a date [cannot have](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/cvt.cpp#L908-L913) a time part, so the Firebird server rejects the cast.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.util.Properties;

public class ClientDialectOne {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 7301 AND 7309");
        doubleQuotedString();
        castAsDate();
        insertDoubleQuotedString();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 7301 AND 7309");
    }

    // Firebird server: "CONSTANT (CHAR): abc"; proxy: "Unknown column 'abc' in 'field list'. [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
    static void doubleQuotedString() {
        printQuery("SELECT \"abc\" FROM RDB$DATABASE");
    }

    // Firebird server: "CAST (TIMESTAMP): 2026-10-15 10:11:12"; proxy: "conversion error from string "2026-10-15 10:11:12""
    static void castAsDate() {
        printQuery("SELECT CAST('2026-10-15 10:11:12' AS DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE");
    }

    // Firebird server: "INSERT: 1 row", "ID = 7302: the row is saved";
    // proxy: "Unknown column 'after' in 'unknown clause'. [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]", "ID = 7302: the row is lost"
    static void insertDoubleQuotedString() throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = connect(); Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            System.out.println("INSERT: " + statement.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (7302, \"after\")") + " row");
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(ex.getMessage());
        }
        printRow(7302);
    }

    // Prints the label, the type and the value of the first column
    static void printQuery(final String sql) {
        try (Connection connection = connect(); Statement statement = connection.createStatement(); ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery(sql)) {
            resultSet.next();
            ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
            System.out.println(metaData.getColumnLabel(1) + " (" + metaData.getColumnTypeName(1) + "): " + resultSet.getString(1));
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // A new connection with SQL dialect 1, auto-commit on
    static Connection connect() throws SQLException {
        Properties properties = new Properties();
        properties.setProperty("user", USER);
        properties.setProperty("password", PASSWORD);
        // Jaybird sends the dialect in op_prepare_statement
        properties.setProperty("sqlDialect", "1");
        return DriverManager.getConnection(URL, properties);
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is lost"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
