### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should accept a connection with the DPB items [`isc_dpb_max_inline_blob_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L136) and [`isc_dpb_max_blob_cache_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L135) in [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5079) as the Firebird server does. If the proxy does not use a DPB item, it should skip it, as the Firebird server [does](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/jrd.cpp#L7330-L7331), instead of rejecting the connection.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects a connection with either of these DPB items, so the client cannot connect. Jaybird [sends](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/internal/StandardConnectionPropertyDefiner.java#L120-L123) the connection property [`maxInlineBlobSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L93) as [`isc_dpb_max_inline_blob_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L136) and [`maxBlobCacheSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L94) as [`isc_dpb_max_blob_cache_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L135).

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, and the rows were read directly from the server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Connect with [`maxInlineBlobSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L93)`=0` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot find code '%d' in dpb type [104]" |
| Insert a row with ID = 8981 without auto-commit, read it and commit | Success | Not executed, there is no connection |
| Connect with [`maxBlobCacheSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L94)`=1000` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot find code '%d' in dpb type [103]" |
| Insert a row with ID = 8982 without auto-commit, read it and commit | Success | Not executed, there is no connection |
| Read the rows with ID = 8981 and ID = 8982 directly on the server | The rows are saved | The rows are lost |

So an application that sets [`maxInlineBlobSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L93) or [`maxBlobCacheSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L94) cannot work through the proxy at all, although it works with the Firebird server.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdAuthenticationEngine#processAttach`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L95-L101) creates [`FirebirdAttachPacket`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/handshake/FirebirdAttachPacket.java#L38-L42), which parses the DPB of [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5079) with [`FirebirdParameterBuffer#parseBuffer`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/constant/buffer/FirebirdParameterBuffer.java#L51-L57). The method [converts](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/constant/buffer/FirebirdParameterBuffer.java#L54) the code of every item to a known type, so one unknown item fails the whole [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5079).
- [`FirebirdDatabaseParameterBufferType`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/constant/buffer/type/FirebirdDatabaseParameterBufferType.java#L35) [ends](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/constant/buffer/type/FirebirdDatabaseParameterBufferType.java#L143-L145) with the codes 100 and 101, and [`FirebirdDatabaseParameterBufferType#valueOf`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/constant/buffer/type/FirebirdDatabaseParameterBufferType.java#L169-L173) throws `NullPointerException` "Cannot find code '%d' in dpb type" for the codes 103 ([`isc_dpb_max_blob_cache_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L135)) and 104 ([`isc_dpb_max_inline_blob_size`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/consts_pub.h#L136)). The proxy answers [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5079) with [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.".
- The Firebird server reads the DPB in [`DatabaseOptions::get`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/jrd.cpp#L6905) and [skips](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/jrd.cpp#L7330-L7331) the items it does not use, so these items do not fail the connection.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.util.Properties;

public class DpbBlobItems {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8981 AND 8982");
        maxInlineBlobSize();
        maxBlobCacheSize();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8981 AND 8982");
    }

    // Firebird server: "connect: success", "INSERT: 1 row", "SELECT: ID = 8981", "COMMIT: success", "ID = 8981: the row is saved";
    // proxy: "connect: Unknown exception." and "More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot find code '%d' in dpb type [104] [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]",
    // "ID = 8981: the row is lost"
    static void maxInlineBlobSize() throws SQLException {
        // Jaybird sends isc_dpb_max_inline_blob_size (104) in op_attach
        session("maxInlineBlobSize", "0", 8981);
    }

    // Firebird server: "connect: success", "INSERT: 1 row", "SELECT: ID = 8982", "COMMIT: success", "ID = 8982: the row is saved";
    // proxy: "connect: Unknown exception." and "More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot find code '%d' in dpb type [103] [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]",
    // "ID = 8982: the row is lost"
    static void maxBlobCacheSize() throws SQLException {
        // Jaybird sends isc_dpb_max_blob_cache_size (103) in op_attach
        session("maxBlobCacheSize", "1000", 8982);
    }

    // Connects with the given connection property, inserts the row without auto-commit, reads it and commits
    static void session(final String property, final String value, final int id) throws SQLException {
        Properties properties = new Properties();
        properties.setProperty("user", USER);
        properties.setProperty("password", PASSWORD);
        properties.setProperty(property, value);
        Connection connection;
        try {
            connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, properties);
            System.out.println("connect: success");
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println("connect: " + ex.getMessage());
            printRow(id);
            return;
        }
        try (connection; Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            System.out.println("INSERT: " + statement.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (" + id + ", '" + value + "')") + " row");
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery("SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
                System.out.println("SELECT: " + (resultSet.next() ? "ID = " + resultSet.getInt(1) : "no row"));
            }
            connection.commit();
            System.out.println("COMMIT: success");
        }
        printRow(id);
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is lost"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

