### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute [`UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6754-L6762) and [`DELETE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6711-L6718) with [`ORDER BY`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6467-L6469) and [`ROWS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6511-L6525) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1` | Success, 0 rows updated | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ORDER'" |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1` | Success, 0 rows deleted | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ORDER'" |
| `UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ROWS 1` | Success, 0 rows updated | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ROWS'" |

So through the proxy an application cannot limit the rows that [`UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6754-L6762) and [`DELETE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6711-L6718) change.

### Reason analysis

- The rules [`update`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L38-L40) and [`delete`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L63-L65) of the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere have no [`ORDER BY`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6467-L6469) and [`ROWS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6511-L6525) clauses, so the proxy rejects these statements with a syntax error.
- The open issue #39956 is about the operands of [`rowsClause`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/BaseRule.g4#L404-L406) in a select statement, which the grammar already accepts, so it does not cover these statements.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class RowLimitClauses {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // Firebird server: "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1 -> update count 0";
            // proxy: "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1 -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ORDER' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1");
            // Firebird server: "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1 -> update count 0";
            // proxy: "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1 -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ORDER' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 ORDER BY ID ROWS 1");
            // Firebird server: "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ROWS 1 -> update count 0";
            // proxy: "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ROWS 1 -> error: Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1ROWS' [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544569]"
            execute(connection, "UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'x' WHERE ID = -1 ROWS 1");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

