### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should accept numbers with an unsigned exponent and no decimal point ([lexer](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L1102-L1112)) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy takes these numbers for column names.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT 1e0 FROM RDB$DATABASE` | One row: 1.0, type [`DOUBLE PRECISION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7735-L7736) | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column '1e0' in 'field list'." |
| `SELECT 1E20 FROM RDB$DATABASE` | One row: 1.0E20, type [`DOUBLE PRECISION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7735-L7736) | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column '1E20' in 'field list'." |

So through the proxy an application cannot use numbers with an unsigned exponent and no decimal point.

### Reason analysis

- [`IDENTIFIER_`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/Literals.g4#L22-L25) may start with a digit and is declared before [`NUMBER_`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/Literals.g4#L31-L33). Both rules match `1e0` with the same length, so ANTLR takes the first rule, and `1e0` becomes an identifier. A number with a signed exponent, such as `1e+5`, is longer as [`NUMBER_`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/Literals.g4#L31-L33) and is read as a number, but the proxy describes it with a wrong type, which #40273 covers.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

2. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class LexerLiterals {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

