### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should name the columns of a derived table after the column list that follows its alias ([`derived_table`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6110-L6120), [`derived_column_list`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6138-L6142)), as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy ignores the column list of the derived table and rejects the column names from it.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT A FROM (SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1) D (A)` | Success, no rows, the column is named A | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column 'A' in 'field list'." |
| `SELECT D.A, D.B FROM (SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1) AS D (A, B)` | Success, no rows, the columns are named A and B | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown column 'D.A' in 'field list'." |

So through the proxy an application cannot rename the columns of a derived table with a column list.

### Reason analysis

- [`tableFactor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L140-L145) in the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere accepts [`columnNames`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/BaseRule.g4#L202-L204) after the alias of a subquery.
- [`FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor#visitTableFactor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor.java#L536-L545) sets only the alias of the [`SubqueryTableSegment`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/segment/generic/table/SubqueryTableSegment.java#L38) and does not add these column names to its [`columns`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/segment/generic/table/SubqueryTableSegment.java#L46).
- [`SubqueryTableSegmentBinder#bind`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/segment/dml/from/type/SubqueryTableSegmentBinder.java#L85-L91) then names the columns of the derived table after the select list of the subquery (`ID`, `NAME`), because the segment has neither columns nor column aliases ([`getSubqueryColumns`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/segment/dml/from/type/SubqueryTableSegmentBinder.java#L100-L113)), so `A` and `D.A` are unknown.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
