### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute [`RECREATE TABLE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1562-L1563), [`SET GENERATOR`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1919-L1930), [`RECREATE SEQUENCE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1578-L1579), [`DROP SEQUENCE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4627-L4628), [`CREATE INDEX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1518-L1529), [`DROP INDEX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4603-L4604), [`RECREATE EXCEPTION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1574-L1575) and [`DROP EXCEPTION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4601-L4602) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error, and [`DROP TABLE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4607-L4608) then fails because the table was not created.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, in this order:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
