The proxy should execute [`CREATE VIEW`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L3791-L3799) and [`DROP VIEW`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4611-L4612) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy answers both statements with an error and does not create the view.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, in this order:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CREATE VIEW V_AUDIT AS SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |
| `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'V_AUDIT'` | 1, the view exists | 0, the view does not exist |
| `DROP VIEW V_AUDIT` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |

So through the proxy an application cannot create or drop a view, and gets only a generic error with a `ClassCastException` or `NullPointerException` in its details.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdDDLStatementVisitor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDDLStatementVisitor.java#L96-L350) does not override `visitCreateView` and `visitDropView`, although the rules [`createView`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DDLStatement.g4#L200-L205) and [`dropView`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DDLStatement.g4#L215-L217) exist and the rule [`execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/autogen/FirebirdStatement.g4#L32-L33) includes them.
- So the visitor builds no statement for them: the default `visitChildren` returns the result of the last child. For `CREATE VIEW V_AUDIT AS SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN` it is the [`SimpleTableSegment`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/FirebirdStatementVisitor.java#L214-L221) of `T_PLAIN`, and [`SQLStatementVisitorEngine#visit`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/api/SQLStatementVisitorEngine.java#L50-L54) fails with `ClassCastException` when it casts it to `SQLStatement`. For `DROP VIEW V_AUDIT` it is `null` from the empty rule [`dropBehaviour`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/BaseRule.g4#L496-L498), and [`SQLBindEngine#bindSQLStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/engine/SQLBindEngine.java#L61-L63) fails with `NullPointerException`. Both exceptions are thrown while [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L117-L119) prepares the statement and reach the client as [`UnknownSQLException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/common/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/exception/generic/UnknownSQLException.java#L30-L32) with the message "Unknown exception."

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class ViewStatements {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // Firebird server: "CREATE VIEW V_AUDIT AS SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN -> update count -1";
            // proxy: "CREATE VIEW V_AUDIT AS SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN -> error: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.ClassCastException: class org.apache.shardingsphere.sql.parser.statement.core.segment.generic.table.SimpleTableSegment cannot be cast to class org.apache.shardingsphere.sql.parser.statement.core.statement.SQLStatement (org.apache.shardingsphere.sql.parser.statement.core.segment.generic.table.SimpleTableSegment and org.apache.shardingsphere.sql.parser.statement.core.statement.SQLStatement are in unnamed module of loader 'app') [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
            execute(connection, "CREATE VIEW V_AUDIT AS SELECT ID, NAME FROM T_PLAIN");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'V_AUDIT' -> COUNT BIGINT: 1";
            // proxy: "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'V_AUDIT' -> COUNT BIGINT: 0"
            execute(connection, "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM RDB$RELATIONS WHERE RDB$RELATION_NAME = 'V_AUDIT'");
            // Firebird server: "DROP VIEW V_AUDIT -> update count -1"; proxy: "DROP VIEW V_AUDIT -> error: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "org.apache.shardingsphere.sql.parser.statement.core.statement.SQLStatement.getDatabaseType()" because "sqlStatement" is null [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
            execute(connection, "DROP VIEW V_AUDIT");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

