### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should reject [`CREATE ROLE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1541), [`GRANT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L932-L937) and [`REVOKE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L1188-L1193) with an error that says that the statement is not supported, as ShardingSphere-Proxy does for DCL statements of other databases in [`ProxyBackendHandlerFactory#checkSupportedSQLStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/handler/ProxyBackendHandlerFactory.java#L161-L171), instead of "Unknown exception."

### Actual behavior

The proxy answers each of these statements with "Unknown exception."

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, in this order:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CREATE ROLE R_AUDIT` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |
| `GRANT SELECT ON T_PLAIN TO R_AUDIT` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |
| `REVOKE SELECT ON T_PLAIN FROM R_AUDIT` | Success | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |

So the application gets "Unknown exception." with a `NullPointerException` in its details instead of an error that tells it that the proxy does not support these statements.

### Reason analysis

- For these statements [`FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor#visitCreateRole`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor.java#L57-L60), [`FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor#visitGrant`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor.java#L45-L49) and [`FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor#visitRevoke`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDCLStatementVisitor.java#L51-L55) build [`CreateRoleStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dcl/role/CreateRoleStatement.java#L26), [`GrantStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dcl/GrantStatement.java#L35) and [`RevokeStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dcl/RevokeStatement.java#L35), which are [`DCLStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/statement/type/dcl/DCLStatement.java#L26) types. [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#getFirebirdStatementTyp