The proxy should return the number of rows changed by an INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE with [`RETURNING`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6822-L6835) in [`isc_info_sql_records`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/dsql.cpp#L916-L920) of [`op_info_sql`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L4709-L4714) as the Firebird server does. Support of the other items of [`op_info_sql`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L4709-L4714) is tracked in #39939. This issue is about [`isc_info_sql_records`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/dsql.cpp#L916-L920), which the proxy already answers, but with a wrong count.

### Actual behavior

The proxy changes the rows and returns the right generated keys, but reports that no row was changed.

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, and the rows were read directly from the server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Insert a row with ID = 8863 with [`prepareStatement(sql, RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS)`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L726-L733) and [`executeUpdate()`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBPreparedStatement.java#L213-L229) | 1 | 0 |
| [`getGeneratedKeys()`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBStatement.java#L436-L443) | ID = 8863, NAME = keys | ID = 8863, NAME = keys |
| Update the row with ID = 8864 the same way | 1 | 0 |
| Delete the row with ID = 8865 the same way | 1 | 0 |
| Commit and read the rows with ID = 8863, 8864 and 8865 directly on the server | The row with ID = 8863 is saved, the row with ID = 8864 is updated, the row with ID = 8865 is deleted | The row with ID = 8863 is saved, the row with ID = 8864 is updated, the row with ID = 8865 is deleted |

So through the proxy an application that checks the update count of a statement with generated keys (for example, an ORM that expects one changed row) decides that the statement failed, although the row is changed.

### Reason analysis

- For [`RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBConnection.java#L726-L733) Jaybird [adds](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/GeneratedKeysQueryBuilder.java#L282-L292) [`RETURNING`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6822-L6835) to the INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE, and [`executeUpdate()`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBPreparedStatement.java#L213-L229) takes the update count from [`isc_info_sql_records`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/dsql.cpp#L916-L920) ([`getUpdateCount`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBStatement.java#L631-L650), [`getSqlCounts`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/AbstractFbStatement.java#L612-L628)).
- The proxy executes the statement with [`RETURNING`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6822-L6835) as a query, and the result is a [`QueryResponseHeader`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/response/header/query/QueryResponseHeader.java#L31). [`FirebirdExecuteStatementCommandExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/execute/FirebirdExecuteStatementCommandExecutor.java#L86-L93) stores the affected rows in [`FirebirdServerPreparedStatement`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/FirebirdServerPreparedStatement.java#L40-L41) only for an [`UpdateResponseHeader`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/response/header/update/UpdateResponseHeader.java#L36), so for this statement the count stays 0.
- [`FirebirdSQLInfoExecutor#getRecordsInfo`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/info/FirebirdSQLInfoExecutor.java#L52-L63) builds [`isc_info_sql_records`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/dsql.cpp#L916-L920) from this count, so the count of changed rows in the answer to [`op_info_sql`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L4709-L4714) is 0. The open PR #40189 changes [`FirebirdSQLInfoExecutor`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/info/FirebirdSQLInfoExecutor.java#L41) (it checks the statement handle), but does not change this count.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.PreparedStatement;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;

public class ReturningUpdateCount {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8863 AND 8865");
        insertWithGeneratedKeys();
        updateAndDeleteWithGeneratedKeys();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8863 AND 8865");
    }

    // Firebird server: "executeUpdate: 1", "getGeneratedKeys: ID = 8863, NAME = keys", "ID = 8863: the row is saved";
    // proxy: "executeUpdate: 0", "getGeneratedKeys: ID = 8863, NAME = keys", "ID = 8863: the row is saved"
    static void insertWithGeneratedKeys() throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            // Jaybird adds RETURNING to the INSERT and reads the update count with op_info_sql
            try (PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (?, ?)", Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS)) {
                statement.setInt(1, 8863);
                statement.setString(2, "keys");
                System.out.println("executeUpdate: " + statement.executeUpdate());
                try (ResultSet keys = statement.getGeneratedKeys()) {
                    System.out.println("getGeneratedKeys: " + (keys.next() ? "ID = " + keys.getInt("ID") + ", NAME = " + keys.getString("NAME") : "no row"));
                }
            }
            connection.commit();
        }
        printRow(8863);
    }

    // Firebird server: "UPDATE executeUpdate: 1", "DELETE executeUpdate: 1", "ID = 8864: NAME = updated", "ID = 8865: no row";
    // proxy: "UPDATE executeUpdate: 0", "DELETE executeUpdate: 0", "ID = 8864: NAME = updated", "ID = 8865: no row"
    static void updateAndDeleteWithGeneratedKeys() throws SQLException {
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8864, 'before')");
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (8865, 'before')");
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            // Jaybird adds RETURNING to the UPDATE and the DELETE too
            try (PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement("UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = ? WHERE ID = ?", Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS)) {
                statement.setString(1, "updated");
                statement.setInt(2, 8864);
                System.out.println("UPDATE executeUpdate: " + statement.executeUpdate());
            }
            try (PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = ?", Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS)) {
                statement.setInt(1, 8865);
                System.out.println("DELETE executeUpdate: " + statement.executeUpdate());
            }
            connection.commit();
        }
        printName(8864);
        printName(8865);
    }

    // Reads the name of the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printName(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "NAME = " + resultSet.getString(1) : "no row"));
        }
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is lost"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

