### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should answer [`op_seek_blob`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5187-L5189) for a BLOB of a query result as the Firebird server does, which allows seek only in a [stream BLOB](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/blb.cpp#L977-L978) and answers with an error for a [segmented BLOB](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/blb.h#L212-L215).

### Actual behavior

The proxy treats every BLOB of a query result as a stream BLOB and executes [`op_seek_blob`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5187-L5189) in a [segmented BLOB](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/blb.h#L212-L215) too.

The row with ID = 9121 was written directly on the Firebird server from a string literal, so its BLOB is segmented. The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT T FROM T_BLOB WHERE ID = 9121`, then [`getBlob(1)`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBResultSet.java#L484) and [`getBytes(4, 3)`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBBlob.java#L342-L371), which [sends](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBBlob.java#L357-L359) [`op_seek_blob`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5187-L5189); the direct connection to the Firebird server has [`maxInlineBlobSize`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L85)`=0`, so that the BLOB is not sent inline | Error [`isc_bad_segstr_type`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/blb.cpp#L977-L978) "invalid BLOB type for operation" | Success, the bytes `333435` ("345") |

So through the proxy an application reads data from a segmented BLOB with seek, while the Firebird server rejects this seek. Jaybird gets the error when the BLOB is not sent inline, as here, and fbclient [rejects](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/client/interface.cpp#L6915-L6919) seek in a segmented BLOB even when the BLOB is sent inline.

The proxy also reports this BLOB as a stream BLOB in [`isc_info_blob_type`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/jrd/inf.cpp#L215-L218) ([`FirebirdBlobInfoExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/info/FirebirdBlobInfoExecutor.java#L50)), so [`FirebirdBlob#isSegmented`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBBlob.java#L320-L327) returns `false` through the proxy and `true` on the Firebird server.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdOpenBlobCommandExecutor#isStreamBlob`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/blob/FirebirdOpenBlobCommandExecutor.java#L87-L92) returns `true` for every BLOB with a negative ID, that is for every BLOB of a query result, and [`FirebirdOpenBlobCommandExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/blob/FirebirdOpenBlobCommandExecutor.java#L63) registers the opened BLOB with this flag. The [class comment](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/blob/FirebirdOpenBlobCommandExecutor.java#L46-L49) says that a result BLOB carries no stored Firebird type, so the real type of the BLOB on the Firebird server is not used. This was chosen in #39984 to make seek usable for query results, although #39051, which #39984 closed, asked to allow seek only in stream BLOBs, as the Firebird server does. The Firebird server keeps the type of a stored BLOB and rejects seek in a segmented one.
- The Firebird frontend cannot get the real type, because the proxy core reads the column with `ResultSet#getObject` ([`StandardDatabaseProxyConnector#getRowData`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/backend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/backend/connector/StandardDatabaseProxyConnector.java#L360), [`JDBCStreamQueryResult#getValue`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/executor/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/executor/sql/execute/result/query/impl/driver/jdbc/type/stream/JDBCStreamQueryResult.java#L127)), and Jaybird returns only the content of the BLOB ([`FBBlobField#getObject`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v5.0.13/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/field/FBBlobField.java#L101-L106)).
- [`FirebirdSeekBlobCommandExecutor#execute`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/blob/FirebirdSeekBlobCommandExecutor.java#L55-L63) throws [`InvalidSegstrTypeException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/exception/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/firebird/exception/protocol/InvalidSegstrTypeException.java#L27) only for a BLOB that is [registered](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/blob/FirebirdSeekBlobCommandExecutor.java#L60) as not stream, so seek in a BLOB of a query result always succeeds.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 5.0.13.

#### Steps

1. Create the table and write the row on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_BLOB (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, B BLOB SUB_TYPE BINARY, T BLOB SUB_TYPE TEXT CHARACTER SET UTF8);
INSERT INTO T_BLOB (ID, T) VALUES (9121, '0123456789');
COMMIT;
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

Jaybird 5.0.13. The code runs the same seek through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server and prints both results. The comments in `main` show what it prints.

```java
import java.sql.Blob;
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.util.HexFormat;
import java.util.Properties;

import org.firebirdsql.jdbc.FirebirdBlob;

public class ResultBlobSeek {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to write the BLOB row and to compare
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_BLOB WHERE ID BETWEEN 9120 AND 9129");
        // A BLOB written from a string literal is a segmented BLOB
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_BLOB (ID, T) VALUES (9121, '0123456789')");
        // Through the proxy: "proxy: isSegmented: false", "proxy: getBytes(4, 3): 333435"
        seekInResultBlob("proxy", URL, USER, PASSWORD, new Properties());
        // Directly on the Firebird server: "Firebird server: isSegmented: true",
        // "Firebird server: getBytes(4, 3): invalid BLOB type for operation [SQLState:42000, ISC error code:335544465]".
        // Inline BLOBs are turned off: otherwise Jaybird reads a small BLOB together with the row
        // and seeks in its own copy without asking the server
        Properties direct = new Properties();
        direct.setProperty("maxInlineBlobSize", "0");
        seekInResultBlob("Firebird server", SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD, direct);
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_BLOB WHERE ID BETWEEN 9120 AND 9129");
    }

    static void seekInResultBlob(final String target, final String url, final String user, final String password, final Properties properties) throws SQLException {
        properties.setProperty("user", user);
        properties.setProperty("password", password);
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(url, properties)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement();
                 ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery("SELECT T FROM T_BLOB WHERE ID = 9121")) {
                resultSet.next();
                Blob blob = resultSet.getBlob(1);
                // The BLOB type from isc_info_blob_type
                System.out.println(target + ": isSegmented: " + ((FirebirdBlob) blob).isSegmented());
                try {
                    // A position greater than 1 makes Jaybird seek in the BLOB
                    System.out.println(target + ": getBytes(4, 3): " + HexFormat.of().formatHex(blob.getBytes(4, 3)));
                } catch (final SQLException ex) {
                    System.out.println(target + ": getBytes(4, 3): " + ex.getMessage());
                }
            }
            connection.commit();
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

