body_text:
### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should reject a login that it cannot complete with a login error, as the Firebird server rejects the login with [`isc_login_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L7590-L7599) when it uses none of the client plugins ([`authPlugins`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L61)). Continuing the login with the next plugin of the client in [`op_cont_auth`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5086-L5090), as the Firebird server [does](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L2118-L2126), is tracked in #39936 and is not part of this issue.

### Actual behavior

When the first plugin of the client is not the SRP plugin of the proxy user, the proxy answers [`op_connect`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5051-L5071) with the name of its own plugin, but then fails on [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5080) with a NullPointerException, and the client gets [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." instead of a login error.

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, each case on a new connection, and the rows were read directly from the Firebird server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Connect with [`authPlugins`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L61)`=Srp256`, insert a row with ID = 8971, commit | Success, the row is saved | Success, the row is saved |
| Connect with [`authPlugins`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L61)`=Srp`, insert a row with ID = 8972, commit | Error [`isc_login_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L7590-L7599) "Error occurred during login, please check server firebird.log for details" | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |
| Connect with [`authPlugins`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L61)`=Srp,Srp256`, insert a row with ID = 8973, commit | Success, the login continues with Srp256 in [`op_cont_auth`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L747-L753), the row is saved | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.", the row is not saved |
| Connect with [`authPlugins`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jaybird/props/PropertyNames.java#L61)`=Srp256,Srp`, insert a row with ID = 8974, commit | Success, the row is saved | Success, the row is saved |

The results above are for the default [`AuthServer = Srp256`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/common/config/config.h#L271) of the Firebird server and the default plugin [`SRP256`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/authenticator/FirebirdAuthenticatorType.java#L38) of the proxy user.

So through the proxy a client that offers no plugin of the proxy, or offers Srp before Srp256, gets [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." with a NullPointerException in the message instead of a login error, and cannot tell it from an internal error of the proxy.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdConnectPacket#getPlugin`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/handshake/FirebirdConnectPacket.java#L113-L115) returns only the first plugin of the client, and [`FirebirdAuthenticationEngine#processConnect`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L135-L142) compares it with the plugin of the proxy user. When they differ, the proxy [answers](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L137-L138) with the name of its plugin and empty data, but does not create [`authData`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L63) (the SRP data of the login) and does not check that the client offers this plugin at all.
- On [`op_attach`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5077-L5080) [`FirebirdAuthenticationEngine#login`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L120-L121) passes the null [`authData`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L63) to [`FirebirdSRPAuthenticator#authenticate`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/authenticator/impl/FirebirdSRPAuthenticator.java#L35-L36), which dereferences it and throws a NullPointerException.
- [`FrontendChannelInboundHandler#failAuthentication`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/netty/FrontendChannelInboundHandler.java#L105-L113) sends this exception to the client through [`FirebirdErrorPacketFactory#newInstance`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/err/FirebirdErrorPacketFactory.java#L44-L47), and [`SQLExceptionTransformEngine#toSQLException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/exception/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/core/SQLExceptionTransformEngine.java#L68) turns it into [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.".
- [`FirebirdAuthenticationEngine#authenticate`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L88-L91) does not implement [`op_cont_auth`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5086-L5090) (the comment [`// TODO implement CONT_AUTH`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/FirebirdAuthenticationEngine.java#L89)), which is tracked in #39936. Until it is implemented, nothing rejects a login that the proxy cannot complete before [`FirebirdSRPAuthenticator#authenticate`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/authentication/authenticator/impl/FirebirdSRPAuthenticator.java#L35-L36) fails.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.util.Properties;

public class AuthPluginList {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8971 AND 8974");
        srp256();
        srp();
        srpThenSrp256();
        srp256ThenSrp();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 8971 AND 8974");
    }

    // Firebird server: "authPlugins=Srp256: ID = 8971: the row is saved"; proxy: "authPlugins=Srp256: ID = 8971: the row is saved"
    static void srp256() throws SQLException {
        loginAndInsert("Srp256", 8971);
    }

    // Firebird server: "authPlugins=Srp: Error occurred during login, please check server firebird.log for details [SQLState:08006, ISC error code:335545106]";
    // proxy: "authPlugins=Srp: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "org.apache.shardingsphere.database.protocol.firebird.packet.handshake.FirebirdSRPAuthenticationData.serverProof(String)" because "authData" is null [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
    static void srp() throws SQLException {
        loginAndInsert("Srp", 8972);
    }

    // Firebird server: "authPlugins=Srp,Srp256: ID = 8973: the row is saved"; proxy: "authPlugins=Srp,Srp256: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "org.apache.shardingsphere.database.protocol.firebird.packet.handshake.FirebirdSRPAuthenticationData.serverProof(String)" because "authData" is null [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
    static void srpThenSrp256() throws SQLException {
        loginAndInsert("Srp,Srp256", 8973);
    }

    // Firebird server: "authPlugins=Srp256,Srp: ID = 8974: the row is saved"; proxy: "authPlugins=Srp256,Srp: ID = 8974: the row is saved"
    static void srp256ThenSrp() throws SQLException {
        loginAndInsert("Srp256,Srp", 8974);
    }

    // Opens a new connection with the given authentication plugins, inserts the row with the given ID and commits
    static void loginAndInsert(final String plugins, final int id) throws SQLException {
        Properties properties = new Properties();
        properties.setProperty("user", USER);
        properties.setProperty("password", PASSWORD);
        // Jaybird offers these plugins in this order and sends the data of the first one in op_connect
        properties.setProperty("authPlugins", plugins);
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, properties)) {
            connection.setAutoCommit(false);
            try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
                statement.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (" + id + ", '" + plugins + "')");
            }
            connection.commit();
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println("authPlugins=" + plugins + ": " + ex.getMessage());
            return;
        }
        printRow(plugins, id);
    }

    // Reads the row directly on the Firebird server
    static void printRow(final String plugins, final int id) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("authPlugins=" + plugins + ": ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? "the row is saved" : "the row is lost"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

