body_text:
### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`8a10a2f4822`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe and return [numeric](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7731-L7750) and [boolean](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7793-L7797) literals in the select list as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy names these columns `CONSTANT`, as the Firebird server does, but describes them with other types, so the client gets wrong values, no row or a broken connection.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT 1.5 FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CONSTANT` of type [NUMERIC](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), value 1.5 | Column `CONSTANT` of type [NUMERIC](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), value 1 |
| `SELECT 1.5e2 FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CONSTANT` of type [DOUBLE PRECISION](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L72), value 150.0 | Column `CONSTANT` of type [NUMERIC](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), value 4639481672377565184 |
| `SELECT FALSE FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CONSTANT` of type [BOOLEAN](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L88), value false | Column `CONSTANT` of type [NULL](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L89), value NULL |
| `SELECT TRUE FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CONSTANT` of type [BOOLEAN](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L88), value true | Column `CONSTANT` of type [NULL](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L89). Jaybird reads the bytes of `true` as the length of a 16 MB value and waits for it. Without a read timeout the statement hangs, with `soTimeout` it fails with [`isc_net_read_err`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/FbExceptionBuilder.java#L301-L305) "Error reading data from the connection." |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9101 AND 9109` | Success | Jaybird error [`jb_connectionClosed`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/FbExceptionBuilder.java#L313-L317) "The connection is closed" |

So through the proxy an application reads wrong values without an error and hangs on [`TRUE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7796).

The open PR #39759 changes how literal columns are described, but does not fix these cases. With its head, `1.5` is still read as 1, `1.5e2` fails with [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.", and Jaybird cannot read the result of `SELECT FALSE`.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#processExpressionProjection`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L424-L437) chooses the type of a literal column by the Java class of the value. `1.5` and `1.5e2` are both [`BigDecimal`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/value/literal/impl/NumberLiteralValue.java#L39-L46) values and get [`Types.NUMERIC`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L433-L434), and a [`Boolean`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/parser/sql/statement/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/statement/core/value/literal/impl/BooleanLiteralValue.java#L36-L38) value keeps the initial [`Types.NULL`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L426).
- [`FirebirdReturnColumnPacket#write`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdReturnColumnPacket.java#L76-L77) always sends scale 0, and [`FirebirdInt8BinaryProtocolValue#write`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdInt8BinaryProtocolValue.java#L37-L38) sends the `BigDecimal` value of the backend result as its [`longValue()`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdInt8BinaryProtocolValue.java#L38), so `1.5` comes as 1.
