### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe a [scalar subquery](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L11238-L11245) in the select list as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes a [scalar subquery](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L11238-L11245) as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), and a [VARCHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L68) value of the subquery breaks the connection.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT (SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `NAME` of type [VARCHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L68), value NULL | Column `(SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1)` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), value NULL |
| Insert a row with ID = 9401 and NAME = 'before' | Success | Success |
| `SELECT (SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 9401) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `NAME` of type [VARCHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L68), value before | Column `(SELECT NAME FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 9401)` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), then Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code 1650812527 in processOperation", the bytes of `befo` |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9401 AND 9409` | Success, 1 row deleted | Jaybird error [`jb_connectionClosed`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/FbExceptionBuilder.java#L313-L317) "The connection is closed" |

So through the proxy an application gets an [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) column instead of [VARCHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L68) for a [scalar subquery](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L11238-L11245) and loses the connection when the subquery returns a text value.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#processReturnValues`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L260-L262) describes every [`SubqueryProjection`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/context/segment/select/projection/impl/SubqueryProjection.java#L39) as [`Types.INTEGER`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L262) and names it by the text of the subquery ([`getColumnName`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/context/segment/select/projection/impl/SubqueryProjection.java#L50-L58)). The open pull request #39759 rewrites this branch, but still describes a subquery as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70). With its head the connection is not broken, but the statement with a text value fails with `isc_random` "Unknown exception."
