### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe and return [`CASE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L13588-L13599), [unary minus](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L8880-L8916) and a [column in parentheses](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L7532-L7535), such as `DISTINCT(RDB$RELATION_ID)`, and a [hexadecimal string literal](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/Parser.cpp#L608-L619) in the select list as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes these statements without output columns, so the client gets no result set.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT CASE WHEN 1 > 0 THEN 'a' ELSE 'b' END FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CASE` of type [CHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L67), value a | No result set, update count 0 |
| `SELECT -RDB$RELATION_ID FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column without a name of type [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), value -N | No result set, update count 0 |
| `SELECT DISTINCT(RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `RDB$RELATION_ID` of type [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), value N | No result set, update count 0 |
| `SELECT (RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `RDB$RELATION_ID` of type [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), value N | No result set, update count 0 |
| `SELECT X'4142' FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CONSTANT` of type [CHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L67), value 0x4142 | No result set, update count 0 |
| With auto-commit off, `INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (9501, 'before')` | Success | Success |
| `SELECT CASE WHEN 1 > 0 THEN 'a' ELSE 'b' END FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `CASE` of type [CHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L67), value a | Jaybird error [`jb_closeCursorBeforeCount`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/AbstractFbStatement.java#L615-L617) "Cursor still open, fetch all rows or close cursor before fetching SQL counts" |

So through the proxy an application gets no row for these statements, and in an open transaction [`Statement.getUpdateCount`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBStatement.java#L631-L649) fails with `jb_closeCursorBeforeCount`.

### Reason analysis

