### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe [`AVG`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L511-L557), [`MIN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) and [`MAX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) in the select list as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes [`AVG`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L511-L557), [`MIN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) and [`MAX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) whatever the type of the argument, so the client gets a number instead of a date or loses the connection.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT MIN(CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `MIN` of type [DATE](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L79), value 2026-10-15 | Column `MIN` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), value 61328 |
| `SELECT MAX(RDB$CHARACTER_SET_NAME) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `MAX` of type [CHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L67), value UTF8 | Column `MAX` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), then Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code 1431586360 in processOperation" |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9601 AND 9609` | Success | Jaybird error [`jb_connectionClosed`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/FbExceptionBuilder.java#L313-L317) "The connection is closed" |
| In a new connection, `SELECT AVG(RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `AVG` of type [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), value N | Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code N in processOperation", where N is the value of the average |

So through the proxy an application gets 61328, the number of days since 1858-11-17, instead of the date 2026-10-15, and [`MAX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) of a string and [`AVG`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L511-L557) close the connection, so an open transaction is lost.

The open PR #39759 changes the types of [`AVG`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L511-L557), [`MIN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) and [`MAX`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L1320-L1323) and fixes `MIN(CURRENT_DATE)`. With its head, however, `AVG` and `MAX` of a system table column are still described as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), because [the argument column is looked up only in the default schema](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/6b86835f8f16b55c5251f9e65143202a1a566fe0/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/prepare/type/aggregate/FirebirdAggregateReturnTypeConverter.java#L56). So `AVG(RDB$RELATION_ID)` is described as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) instead of [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), and `MAX(RDB$CHARACTER_SET_NAME)` fails with [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.". `MAX(NAME)` of the `VARCHAR(20)` column of `T_PLAIN` is described with the length 255.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#processReturnValues`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L257-L259) describes an [`AggregationProjection`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/binder/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/binder/context/segment/select/projection/impl/AggregationProjection.java#L44) by the function name only. [`getFunctionType`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L434-L450) has no case for `avg`, `min` and `max`, so they get the [default](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L447-L448) [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) type whatever the type of the argument.
- [`FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder#build`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder.java#L46) encodes the row by the type of the backend result. The [DATE](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L79) value is read as the described [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), and the [CHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L67) and [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80) values take more bytes than the described [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), so Jaybird reads the rest of the value as the next operation code ([`processOperation`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205)) and closes the connection. The operation code 1431586360 is the bytes of `UTF8`, and the operation code N is the value of [`AVG`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/AggNodes.cpp#L511-L557).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" in this order through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. The value of `RDB$RELATION_ID` depends on the database. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.sql.Types;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class AggregateDescribe {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // The value is the current date. Firebird server: "SELECT MIN(CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> MIN DATE: 2026-10-15";
            // proxy: "SELECT MIN(CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> MIN INTEGER: 61328"
            execute(connection, "SELECT MIN(CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE");
            // Firebird server: "SELECT MAX(RDB$CHARACTER_SET_NAME) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> MAX CHAR(63): UTF8" with spaces up to 63 characters;
            // proxy: "SELECT MAX(RDB$CHARACTER_SET_NAME) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> error: Unsupported or unexpected operation code 1431586360 in processOperation [SQLState:08000, ISC error code:337248276]"
            execute(connection, "SELECT MAX(RDB$CHARACTER_SET_NAME) FROM RDB$DATABASE");
            // Firebird server: "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9601 AND 9609 -> update count 0";
            // proxy: "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9601 AND 9609 -> error: The connection is closed [SQLState:08006, ISC error code:337248336]"
            execute(connection, "DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9601 AND 9609");
        }
        // A new connection: through the proxy the first one is closed
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD)) {
            // N is the value of RDB$RELATION_ID. Firebird server: "SELECT AVG(RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> AVG BIGINT: N";
            // proxy: "SELECT AVG(RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE -> error: Unsupported or unexpected operation code N in processOperation ..."
            execute(connection, "SELECT AVG(RDB$RELATION_ID) FROM RDB$DATABASE");
        }
    }

    // Executes the statement and prints the described columns with the rows, the update count or the error
    static void execute(final Connection connection, final String sql) {
        try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
            if (!statement.execute(sql)) {
                System.out.println(sql + " -> update count " + statement.getUpdateCount());
                return;
            }
            try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.getResultSet()) {
                ResultSetMetaData metaData = resultSet.getMetaData();
                List<String> columns = new ArrayList<>();
                for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                    int type = metaData.getColumnType(i);
                    boolean text = Types.CHAR == type || Types.VARCHAR == type;
                    columns.add(metaData.getColumnLabel(i) + " " + metaData.getColumnTypeName(i) + (text ? "(" + metaData.getPrecision(i) + ")" : ""));
                }
                List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();
                while (resultSet.next()) {
                    List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (int i = 1; i <= metaData.getColumnCount(); i++) {
                        values.add(String.valueOf(resultSet.getObject(i)));
                    }
                    rows.add(String.join(", ", values));
                }
                System.out.println(sql + " -> " + String.join(", ", columns) + ": " + (rows.isEmpty() ? "no rows" : String.join("; ", rows)));
            }
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + " -> error: " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

