### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should return and save [`TIME WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4837-L4845) values with their time zone, as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy answers both a [`TIME WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4837-L4845) result and a [`TIME WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4837-L4845) parameter with an error.

The same steps were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, the values were read with [`getString`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBResultSet.java#L452-L454), and the saved rows were read directly from the Firebird server:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT TMZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911`, the value is `10:11:12.3456 +03:00` | `10:11:12.345600+03:00` | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception." |
| Insert a row with ID = 8914 and TMZ = `10:11:12+03:00`, an `OffsetTime` parameter of [`setObject`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/jdbc/FBPreparedStatement.java#L312-L314) | Success, the row is saved with the time `10:11:12.0000 +03:00` | Error [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception.", the row is not saved |

So through the proxy an application cannot read or write [`TIME WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4837-L4845) values at all, and gets only a generic error with an `IllegalArgumentException` in its details.

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdBinaryProtocolValueFactory`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdBinaryProtocolValueFactory.java#L38-L53) registers no value for [`TIME_TZ`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/FirebirdBinaryColumnType.java#L61), so [`FirebirdBinaryProtocolValueFactory#getBinaryProtocolValue`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/protocol/FirebirdBinaryProtocolValueFactory.java#L140-L143) throws `IllegalArgumentException` for [`TIME WITH TIME ZONE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L4837-L4845). [`SQLExceptionTransformEngine#toSQLException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/exception/core/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/exception/core/SQLExceptionTransformEngine.java#L68) turns it into [`UnknownSQLException`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/infra/common/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/infra/exception/generic/UnknownSQLException.java#L31) "Unknown exception.".
  - For a parameter, the exception is thrown while [`FirebirdExecuteStatementPacket`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/command/query/statement/execute/FirebirdExecuteStatementPacket.java#L77-L81) reads the [`op_execute`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5243-L5246) packet, and [`FirebirdPacketCodecEngine#decode`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/codec/FirebirdPacketCodecEngine.java#L81-L91) answers with the error and closes the connection.
  - For a result, the exception is thrown while [`FirebirdFetchResponsePacket`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/packet/generic/FirebirdFetchResponsePacket.java#L61-L64) writes the row for [`op_fetch`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/remote/server/server.cpp#L5253-L5256), and [`FirebirdPacketCodecEngine#encode`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/database/protocol/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/database/protocol/firebird/codec/FirebirdPacketCodecEngine.java#L212-L215) writes the error instead of the row.

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table and the rows on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_DTZ (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, TMZ TIME WITH TIME ZONE, TSZ TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE);
INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8911, TIME '10:11:12.3456 +03:00', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12.3456 -05:30');
INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8912, TIME '23:59:59 Europe/Moscow', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12 America/Sao_Paulo');
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the steps from the table under "Actual behavior" through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

All cases on Jaybird 6.0.7, one method per case. The comment above each method shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.PreparedStatement;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.sql.Statement;
import java.time.OffsetDateTime;
import java.time.OffsetTime;
import java.time.ZoneOffset;

public class TimeWithTimeZone {

    // The proxy; put the URL, user and password of the Firebird server here to compare
    static final String URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<proxy host>:<proxy port>/firebird_db?encoding=UTF8&wireCrypt=DISABLED";

    static final String USER = "root";

    static final String PASSWORD = "root";

    // The Firebird server, to write and read the rows directly
    static final String SERVER_URL = "jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>";

    static final String SERVER_USER = "<user>";

    static final String SERVER_PASSWORD = "<password>";

    public static void main(final String[] args) throws Exception {
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID BETWEEN 8911 AND 8914");
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8911, TIME '10:11:12.3456 +03:00', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12.3456 -05:30')");
        executeOnServer("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, TMZ, TSZ) VALUES (8912, TIME '23:59:59 Europe/Moscow', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-15 10:11:12 America/Sao_Paulo')");
        // One connection per case: after the error on a TIME WITH TIME ZONE parameter the proxy closes the connection
        selectTime();
        insertTime();
        executeOnServer("DELETE FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID BETWEEN 8911 AND 8914");
    }

    // Firebird server: "SELECT TMZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911: 10:11:12.345600+03:00";
    // proxy: "SELECT TMZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Cannot find Firebird type 'TIME_TZ' in column type when process binary protocol value [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]"
    static void selectTime() {
        printSelect("SELECT TMZ FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = 8911");
    }

    // Firebird server: "Insert ID = 8914: success", "ID = 8914: 10:11:12.0000 +03:00";
    // proxy: "Insert ID = 8914: Unknown exception. More details: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Cannot find Firebird type 'TIME_TZ' in column type when process binary protocol value [SQLState:HY000, ISC error code:335544382]", "ID = 8914: the row is not saved"
    static void insertTime() throws SQLException {
        insert(8914, "TMZ", OffsetTime.of(10, 11, 12, 0, ZoneOffset.ofHours(3)));
        printSaved(8914, "TMZ");
    }

    // Executes the query through the proxy and prints the value as a string
    static void printSelect(final String sql) {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD);
             Statement statement = connection.createStatement();
             ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery(sql)) {
            resultSet.next();
            System.out.println(sql + ": " + resultSet.getString(1));
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println(sql + ": " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // Inserts the row through the proxy with the value as a parameter
    static void insert(final int id, final String column, final Object value) {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(URL, USER, PASSWORD);
             PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement("INSERT INTO T_DTZ (ID, " + column + ") VALUES (?, ?)")) {
            statement.setInt(1, id);
            statement.setObject(2, value);
            statement.executeUpdate();
            System.out.println("Insert ID = " + id + ": success");
        } catch (final SQLException ex) {
            System.out.println("Insert ID = " + id + ": " + ex.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // Reads the time and the time zone of the saved value directly on the Firebird server
    static void printSaved(final int id, final String column) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD);
             ResultSet resultSet = connection.createStatement().executeQuery(
                     "SELECT CAST(CAST(" + column + " AS TIME WITH TIME ZONE) AS VARCHAR(60)) FROM T_DTZ WHERE ID = " + id)) {
            System.out.println("ID = " + id + ": " + (resultSet.next() ? resultSet.getString(1) : "the row is not saved"));
        }
    }

    static void executeOnServer(final String sql) throws SQLException {
        try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection(SERVER_URL, SERVER_USER, SERVER_PASSWORD)) {
            connection.createStatement().execute(sql);
        }
    }
}
```

