### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should execute [`SELECT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5781-L5792), [`UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6758) and [`DELETE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6714) with [`PLAN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6370-L6373) as the Firebird server does.

### Actual behavior

The proxy rejects each of these statements with a syntax error.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, in one transaction with auto-commit off, after inserting a row with ID = 6701:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 PLAN (T_PLAIN NATURAL)` | The row with ID = 6701 | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = 6701 PLAN (T_PLAIN NATURAL), null" |
| `UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'updated' WHERE ID = 6701 PLAN (T_PLAIN NATURAL)` | Success, 1 row updated | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: UPDATE T_PLAIN SET NAME = 'updated' WHERE ID = 6701 PLAN (T_PLAIN NATURAL), null" |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 PLAN (T_PLAIN NATURAL)` | Success, no rows deleted | Error [`isc_dsql_error`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L250) "Dynamic SQL Error; You have an error in your SQL syntax: no viable alternative at input '-1PLAN'" |

So through the proxy an application cannot give a query or a data change its access plan.

### Reason analysis

- The rule [`selectClause`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L79-L81) of the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere has no [`PLAN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6370-L6373), and the grammar has no `PLAN` token, so the proxy rejects these statements with a syntax error.
- The rules [`update`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L38-L40) and [`delete`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/DMLStatement.g4#L63-L65) have no `PLAN` either. The Firebird server allows [`PLAN`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6370-L6373) in a [query specification](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L5998), in [`DELETE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6714), [`UPDATE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6758), [`MERGE`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6631) and [`UPDATE OR INSERT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L6802).

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Turn auto-commit off, execute `INSERT INTO T_PLAIN (ID, NAME) VALUES (6701, 'before')` and then the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" in the same transaction through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

The statements from the table on Jaybird 6.0.7. The comment above each call shows what it prints against the Firebird server and through the proxy.

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.ResultSetMetaData;
import java.sql.SQLException;
