### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`01446d4fad4`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe a [`UNION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/pass1.cpp#L2550-L2565) column in the select list as the Firebird server does, which takes the type from [all branches](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/pass1.cpp#L2548-L2566).

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes a [`UNION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/pass1.cpp#L2550-L2565) column by its first branch as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), and the [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80) value of the second branch breaks the connection.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT ID FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID = -1 UNION ALL SELECT CAST(1 AS BIGINT) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `ID` of type [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80), value 1 | Column `ID` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), then Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code 1 in processOperation" |
| `DELETE FROM T_PLAIN WHERE ID BETWEEN 9401 AND 9409` | Success | Jaybird error [`jb_connectionClosed`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/FbExceptionBuilder.java#L313-L317) "The connection is closed" |

So through the proxy an application loses the connection on a [`UNION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/pass1.cpp#L2550-L2565) of [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) and [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80).

### Reason analysis

- [`FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor#visitCombineClause`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/sql/parser/engine/firebird/visitor/statement/type/FirebirdDMLStatementVisitor.java#L285) builds the [`UNION`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/pass1.cpp#L2550-L2565) statement with the projections of the first branch, and [`getProjections`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L267-L273) returns them for the description, so [`processReturnValues`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L246-L254) gives the column the type of `T_PLAIN.ID`.
- [`FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder#build`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/01446d4fad48450e7fc3eb3b3631b25d6bf411df/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder.java#L46) encodes the row by the type of the backend result, so the 8-byte [BIGINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L80) value is sent under the described 4-byte [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) column. Jaybird reads the rest of the value as the next operation code ([`processOperation`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205)) and closes the connection.
