### Before reporting a bug

- [x] I have searched open and closed [GitHub issues](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/issues).
- [x] I have read the [ShardingSphere documentation](https://shardingsphere.apache.org/document/current/en/overview).

### ShardingSphere version

master, commit [`8a10a2f4822`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/commit/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2)

### ShardingSphere project

ShardingSphere-Proxy

### Expected behavior

The proxy should describe [`EXTRACT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L8198-L8200) in the select list as the Firebird server [does](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/ExprNodes.cpp#L5459-L5485): `MILLISECOND` as NUMERIC(9,1), `TIMEZONE_NAME` as VARCHAR(32) and the other date parts as SMALLINT.

### Actual behavior

The proxy describes [`EXTRACT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L8198-L8200) with the date parts `WEEKDAY`, `YEARDAY`, `MILLISECOND` and `TIMEZONE_NAME` as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), and the values of `MILLISECOND` and `TIMEZONE_NAME` break the connection.

The same statements were executed directly on the Firebird server and through the proxy, each on a new connection:

| Steps | Firebird server | Proxy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT EXTRACT(WEEKDAY FROM CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `EXTRACT` of type [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), the day of the week | Column `EXTRACT` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), the same value |
| `SELECT EXTRACT(YEARDAY FROM CURRENT_DATE) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `EXTRACT` of type [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), the day of the year | Column `EXTRACT` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), the same value |
| `SELECT EXTRACT(MILLISECOND FROM CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `EXTRACT` of type NUMERIC(9,1), the milliseconds | Column `EXTRACT` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), then Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code N in processOperation" |
| `SELECT EXTRACT(TIMEZONE_NAME FROM CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) FROM RDB$DATABASE` | Column `EXTRACT` of type [VARCHAR](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L68)(32), the name of the time zone | Column `EXTRACT` of type [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70), then Jaybird error [`jb_unexpectedOperationCode`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205) "Unsupported or unexpected operation code N in processOperation" |

So through the proxy an application gets wrong column types for [`EXTRACT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L8198-L8200) and loses the connection on `EXTRACT(MILLISECOND …)` and `EXTRACT(TIMEZONE_NAME …)`.

### Reason analysis

- The lexer of the Firebird grammar of ShardingSphere has no tokens for the date parts `WEEKDAY`, `YEARDAY`, `MILLISECOND` and `TIMEZONE_NAME`, so they are read as identifiers, which [`extractFunction`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/parser/sql/engine/dialect/firebird/src/main/antlr4/imports/firebird/BaseRule.g4#L333-L335) accepts, and the statement is parsed as a function call.
- [`FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor#getFunctionType`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L440-L456) has no branch for [`EXTRACT`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/dsql/parse.y#L8198-L8200), so its [`default`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/prepare/FirebirdPrepareStatementCommandExecutor.java#L453-L454) branch describes the column as [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70).
- [`FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder#build`](https://github.com/apache/shardingsphere/blob/8a10a2f4822841b45561796ad02c4709ae69e2e2/proxy/frontend/dialect/firebird/src/main/java/org/apache/shardingsphere/proxy/frontend/firebird/command/query/statement/FirebirdBinaryRowBuilder.java#L43-L49) encodes the row by the type of the backend result, so the NUMERIC value of `MILLISECOND` and the VARCHAR value of `TIMEZONE_NAME` are sent under the described 4-byte [INTEGER](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L70) column. Jaybird reads the rest of the value as the next operation code ([`processOperation`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/jaybird/blob/v6.0.7/src/main/org/firebirdsql/gds/ng/wire/AbstractWireOperations.java#L201-L205)) and closes the connection.
- With the head of the open pull request #39759 the date parts are described as [SMALLINT](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/sqlda_pub.h#L69), and the connection is not broken, but `EXTRACT(MILLISECOND …)` and `EXTRACT(TIMEZONE_NAME …)` fail with [`isc_random`](https://github.com/FirebirdSQL/firebird/blob/v5.0.4/src/include/firebird/impl/msg/jrd.h#L63) "Unknown exception."

### Steps to reproduce

#### Environment

- Firebird server 5.0.
- Client: Jaybird 6.0.7.

#### Steps

1. Create the table on the Firebird server:

```sql
CREATE TABLE T_PLAIN (ID INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, NAME VARCHAR(20));
```

2. Start ShardingSphere-Proxy with this configuration:

```yaml
# global.yaml
authority:
  users:
    - user: root@%
      password: root
  privilege:
    type: ALL_PERMITTED
props:
  proxy-frontend-database-protocol-type: Firebird
```

```yaml
# database-firebird.yaml
databaseName: firebird_db
dataSources:
  ds_0:
    url: jdbc:firebirdsql://<host>/<database file>?encoding=UTF8
    username: <user>
    password: <password>
rules:
  - !SINGLE
    tables:
      - "*.*"
```

3. Execute the statements from the table under "Actual behavior" in this order through the proxy and directly on the Firebird server, and compare the results. The value N of `RDB$RELATION_ID` depends on the database. "Example code" runs all of them.

### Example code

